comments.body:
NIT: current `BindAddress` keeps the address as a string, and `InitHTTPServer` parses it later with Lookup. This "late" lookup has the consequence that an invalid `-rpcbind` value is only detected inside the bind loop. Resulting that possible earlier endpoints may already be listening, and `StopListening()` has to undo them. 

I think we can do this lookup (with fAllowLookup=false) sooner, as  pure numeric parse without DNS (So it is safe to call it in `GetBindAddresses`) and store it typed. This is the same way the lookup is done in the bind loop.
This has the benefit that any invalid -rpcbind address fails before any socket is opened, equal to the `port` logic.  And, to me, failing fast without the "risk" of opening sockets, is the better security posture. 

